                            <comment id="16510976" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 13 Jun 2018 11:41:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user prabhjyotsingh opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3018&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3018&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3539&quot; title=&quot;Add jceks stored password support for LDAP&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-3539&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-3539&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Add jceks stored password support for LDAP&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    This is to add support for storing password in jceks for LDAP (realm).&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;    If the hadoopSecurityCredentialPath path is present and not empty in the shiro.ini, then the password is read from the keystore file and it need not be stored inside the shiro.ini file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What type of PR is it?&lt;br/&gt;
