&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3539&quot; title=&quot;Add jceks stored password support for LDAP&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-3539&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-3539&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;(&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3539&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3539&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;How should this be tested?&lt;br/&gt;
    Create a keystore file using the hadoop credential command line&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    hadoop credential create ldapRealm.systemPassword -provider jceks://file/user/zeppelin/conf/zeppelin.jceks&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    Change the following values in the Shiro.ini file, and uncomment the line:&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    ldapRealm.hadoopSecurityCredentialPath = jceks://file/user/zeppelin/conf/zeppelin.jceks&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;



